# The Bigger Reason This Matters

Right now your brain is still building:

* syntax recognition
* programming fluency
* problem-solving patterns
* understanding of data types
* understanding methods
* confidence writing code from memory

This is exactly the area you said you struggle with:

> “I can read code but struggle writing from scratch.”

These exercises help fix that.

Because eventually you stop thinking:

```text
“How do I reverse a string again?”
```

and your brain instantly knows:

```ruby
.reverse
```

That frees mental energy for:

* architecture
* debugging
* APIs
* databases
* React
* Rails
* interview problems

---

# Think of It Like Basketball Fundamentals

A professional basketball player still practices:

* dribbling
* layups
* footwork
* shooting form

Even though those are “basic.”

Why?

Because advanced gameplay is built on automatic fundamentals.

Programming is the same.

Rails apps, APIs, React frontends, databases — they all sit on top of:

* variables
* strings
* arrays
* loops
* methods
* conditionals

That’s why this practice matters.
